# Git LFS: the built-in slice heads are large binary blobs (~364 MiB total,
# 340 files). Tracking them through LFS keeps ordinary clones small while the
# full payload stays part of the repository history.
*.part filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
# Never normalise line endings in binary payloads.
*.ipa binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.mp3 binary
*.mp4 binary
